  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">06 — Special Symbol Family</h2>
    <h3 class="section-sub">Concepts drawn from the mark's own geometry</h3>

    <p class="lede">
      Twelve marks built from the same circle / cut / node vocabulary as the
      primary logo, for use as decorative or status glyphs inside the product —
      never as generic clip-art.
    </p>

    <div class="sym-grid">

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi" style="width:30px;height:30px;color:var(--text)">
          <use href="#ozl-mark"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Intelligence</div>
        <div class="desc">the primary mark itself</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-insight"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Insight</div>
        <div class="desc">a single point of light inside the whole</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-research"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Research</div>
        <div class="desc">a field being scanned</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-discovery"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Discovery</div>
        <div class="desc">a node found beyond the known edge</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-creation"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Creation</div>
        <div class="desc">the cut itself, isolated</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-conversation"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Conversation</div>
        <div class="desc">two fields, overlapping</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-sources"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Sources</div>
        <div class="desc">references fanning from one point</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-active"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Active state</div>
        <div class="desc">a filled core within its field</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-thinking"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Thinking state</div>
        <div class="desc">possibilities clustering</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-processing"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Processing state</div>
        <div class="desc">motion around the field</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-success"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Success</div>
        <div class="desc">confirmation within the field</div>
      </div>

      <div class="sym-tile">
        <svg class="oi">
          <use href="#sym-warning"></use>
        </svg>
        <div class="label">Warning</div>
        <div class="desc">attention within the field</div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">07 — Source Publisher Marks</h2>
    <h3 class="section-sub">Container system, not redrawn trademarks</h3>

    <p class="lede">
      OZLIND never redraws a publisher's logo. This defines the compact
      <em>container</em> a real, licensed publisher mark drops into — plus the
      neutral fallback icon used whenever one isn't available. The labelled
      squares below are placeholder slots for layout only, not brand
      reproductions.
    </p>

    <div class="source-row">
      <div class="src-slot">CNN</div>
      <div class="src-slot">BBC</div>
      <div class="src-slot">AP</div>
      <div class="src-overflow">+4</div>
    </div>

    <p class="src-note">
      Each slot: 30×30px, 9px corner radius, neutral surface fill. A real
      integration renders the publisher's own official mark inside the same slot
      (via favicon/brand API where licensed) — OZLIND supplies the frame, spacing
      and overflow behaviour, never the artwork.
    </p>

    <div class="src-expand">
      <div class="src-slot">NYT</div>

      <div class="src-expand-meta">
        <div class="title">
          Why researchers are re-testing an old idea
        </div>
        <div class="domain">nytimes.com</div>
      </div>

      <svg class="openicon">
        <use href="#i-open-external"></use>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <p class="src-note" style="margin-top:10px">
      Tapping a slot expands to this row — title, domain and an open-link action —
      instead of long inline text labels crowding the answer.
    </p>

    <div class="fallback-row">

      <div class="src-slot">
        <svg>
          <use href="#src-fallback"></use>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <p class="src-note" style="margin-top:0">
        Neutral OZLIND Source glyph — used whenever a publisher's mark can't be
        retrieved. Built from the same circle-and-chord language as the rest of
        the system, so it never reads as a broken image.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">08 — Usage &amp; Naming</h2>
    <h3 class="section-sub">How the kit is organised</h3>

    <table class="naming">

      <tr>
        <th>Asset</th>
        <th>ID convention</th>
        <th>Example</th>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>Primary mark</td>
        <td><code>ozl-*</code></td>
        <td><code>ozl-mark</code>, <code>ozl-node</code></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>UI icons</td>
        <td><code>i-*</code></td>
        <td><code>i-send</code>, <code>i-documents</code></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>Special symbols</td>
        <td><code>sym-*</code></td>
        <td><code>sym-thinking</code>, <code>sym-sources</code></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>Source system</td>
        <td><code>src-*</code></td>
        <td><code>src-fallback</code></td>
      </tr>

    </table>

    <div class="code-box">&lt;!-- paste the sprite once, then reference anywhere --&gt;
&lt;svg class="oi"&gt;&lt;use href="#i-send"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;

/* icons inherit colour from CSS — no separate light/dark files */
.oi { color: var(--text); }
.oi:hover { color: var(--accent); }</div>

    <div class="dodont" style="margin-top:34px;">

      <div class="col do">
        <h4>Do</h4>

        <ul>
          <li>Keep the mark's clear space equal to its own node width</li>
          <li>Use the accent node only once per view as a focal point</li>
          <li>Let icons inherit <code>currentColor</code> for theme switching</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="col dont">
        <h4>Don't</h4>

        <ul>
          <li>Add drop shadows, gradients or bevels to the mark</li>
          <li>Recolour individual strokes within one icon</li>
          <li>Redraw or approximate a publisher's own logo</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="wrap">
    OZLIND Visual Identity System — primary mark, wordmark, 49-icon family,
    12-symbol family and source-mark container system, drawn as one coherent
    geometry. Owned by Athul.
  </footer>

</div>

</body>
</html>
